.TH geectl-build-job-status 1  "geectl-build-job-status 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-job\-status \- Read the running build job for a package, if any
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build job\-status\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the running build job for a package, if any
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to read the job for
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the package builds in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the package builds for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
